diff --git a/docs/configuration.rst b/docs/configuration.rst
index 101e050..8b67b29 100644
--- a/docs/configuration.rst
+++ b/docs/configuration.rst
@@ -144,9 +144,20 @@ The event-posting can be disabled completely (the default is to be enabled):
     def configure(settings: kopf.OperatorSettings, **_):
         settings.posting.enabled = False
 
+The posting of the log messages (but not of the explicit `kopf.event` and
+similar calls) can be disabled separately:
+
+.. code-block:: python
+
+    import kopf
+
+    @kopf.on.startup()
+    def configure(settings: kopf.OperatorSettings, **_):
+        settings.posting.loggers = False
+
 .. note::
 
-    These settings also affect `kopf.event` and related functions:
+    The ``enabled`` and ``level`` settings also affect `kopf.event` and related functions:
     `kopf.info`, `kopf.warn`, `kopf.exception`, etc --
     even if they are called explicitly in the code.
 
